{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the nested scalar likelihood statements `y[n, t] ~ normal(...)` with a single top-level vectorized observation `y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y)`. The helper array `y_hat` is filled in the model block after all parameter priors, so the protected data variable `y` is observed exactly once with a plain sampling statement. No data fields were added; `data_safe.json` is the supplied data unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"// http://www.mrc-bsu.cam.ac.uk/bugs/winbugs/Vol1.pdf
// Page 3: Rats
data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  int<lower=0> T;
  array[T] real x;
  array[N, T] real y;
  real xbar;
}
parameters {
  array[N] real alpha;
  array[N] real beta;

  real mu_alpha;
  real mu_beta; // beta.c in original bugs model

  real<lower=0> sigmasq_y;
  real<lower=0> sigmasq_alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigmasq_beta;
}
transformed parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma_y; // sigma in original bugs model
  real<lower=0> sigma_alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma_beta;

  sigma_y = sqrt(sigmasq_y);
  sigma_alpha = sqrt(sigmasq_alpha);
  sigma_beta = sqrt(sigmasq_beta);
}
model {
  array[N, T] real y_hat;

  mu_alpha ~ normal(0, 100);
  mu_beta ~ normal(0, 100);
  sigmasq_y ~ inv_gamma(0.001, 0.001);
  sigmasq_alpha ~ inv_gamma(0.001, 0.001);
  sigmasq_beta ~ inv_gamma(0.001, 0.001);
  alpha ~ normal(mu_alpha, sigma_alpha); // vectorized
  beta ~ normal(mu_beta, sigma_beta); // vectorized
  for (n in 1 : N) {
    for (t in 1 : T) {
      y_hat[n, t] = alpha[n] + beta[n] * (x[t] - xbar);
    }
  }
  y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y);
}
generated quantities {
  real alpha0;
  alpha0 = mu_alpha - xbar * mu_beta;
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":4,"T":4,"x":[5.8514287980475395,6.804849405681604,3.4170016987335643,6.686066338078085],"xbar":3.929841926471559,"y":[[4.0,2.0,3.0,4.0],[4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0],[3.0,3.0,4.0,2.0],[2.0,4.0,4.0,3.0]]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
